# Human-in-the-Loop AI Documentation Lifecycle Workflow

## Workflow Philosophy
Artificial Intelligence is a powerful optimization accelerator, not an absolute automated author. This document defines our human-in-the-loop lifecycle, ensuring that all AI-generated technical content undergoes strict engineering verification, structural validation, and stylistic editing before reaching production branches.

## Integrated AI Content Lifecycle Pipeline

```text
[Raw Source Material / Jira Data]
               │
               ▼
   [Context & Prompt Injection] ───> (Enterprise LLM Processing Engine)
               │
               ▼
   [Draft Post-Processing] ────────> (Automated Style/Syntax Linting)
               │
               ▼
   [Human Content Review] ─────────> (Technical Accuracy & Tone Verification)
               │
               ▼
[Production Branch Deployment]
```

## Step-by-Step Execution Phases

### Phase 1: Context Gathering & Prompt Preparation
Writers extract raw technical inputs from Jira user stories, developer code comments, or recorded technical review sessions. This data is combined with standardized organizational templates to establish explicit context boundaries.

### Phase 2: Assisted Content Assembly
The structured data is processed using approved enterprise Large Language Models (LLMs) to generate initial structural drafts, step-by-step instructions, or API resource outlines.

### Phase 3: Automated Formatting & Quality Controls
Drafts are immediately committed to a local staging environment where automated linters run programmatic validation checks:
* **Style Guidelines Check:** Verifies structural tone and voice rules using `Vale`.
* **Structural Lint Check:** Validates formatting, tags, and syntax trees via `markdownlint`.

### Phase 4: Human-Centric Peer Review
A Senior Technical Writer conducts an intensive editorial review to confirm that the text flows naturally, uses active voice, matches target personas, and contains zero factual anomalies. A Subject Matter Expert (SME) then performs an engineering verification pass to guarantee accuracy.
